# Exact cached post-live --all findings; answers explain only the anchors of their class.

[thin] These exact 1.12 mm readings bound the outer footer stock above the source wing-slot exit: manufacturing Z 2.38 to Z 3.50. The slot retains the complete grip span and 1.68 mm wing with 0.45 mm retaining air. The receiver itself retains 3.00 mm end walls and 12.00 mm stock above the slot within those walls; the added outer footer is a separate storage adaptation. The exit stays open for source-wing insertion and support cleanup. This local footer web has no physical handling-load or lifetime acceptance.
alternatives: A 4.50 mm outer footer gives 2.12 mm above the same slot, and a 5.38 mm footer gives 3.00 mm; either enlarges the side module and needs its storage/removal access reviewed. Trimming the footer away from the wing exit eliminates this local web but reduces the storage bridge. Closing the exit fills the opening but changes the represented source-wing access and support-removal geometry.
