[thin] These exact pairs bound 3.00 mm receiver back-web or end-wall stock. The back web runs manufacturing Y 6.00–9.00; the end walls are X 40.00–43.00 and X -43.00–-40.00. The full source wing slots and span remain in those end walls. This is ordinary connected receiver stock rather than a clearance rung or flexible calibration wall. The vertical reference has no physical load, stiffness or handling-life qualification.
alternatives: A 4.00 or 6.00 mm back web can grow outward while keeping its inner face, but enlarges the side module and needs a new dock/removal review. Thicker end walls increase wing-slot engagement length and change the source receiver section unless the new stock stays beyond its original span. Separate broad receiver blocks use more material and another alignment joint instead of this full-span web.
