[ledge] This underside belongs to the downward-open lower storage channel in the added GR footer, not a source grip retaining surface. In the manufacturing pose its roof is Z 2.30 over a 4.30 mm Y bridge span, leaving 1.20 mm solid stock to the footer top Z 3.50. The channel is open through the footer bottom and along the world -X withdrawal path. Current native first roof nozzle Z 2.60 has 6 Bridge and 2 Overhang-wall deposits with no channel support, followed by solid infill at Z 2.84. The assembled rooted P key preserves 0.15 mm nominal Y air per side and 0.27 mm nominal top air; physical release and handling force remain unmeasured.
alternatives: A 4.50 or 5.30 mm manufacturing footer provides 2.20 or 3.00 mm roof stock over the same channel, but grows the outboard module and needs its grip access and withdrawal envelope reviewed. A separately bedded socket cap removes this bridge while adding an attachment/alignment joint. Opening through the roof removes the local roof but changes the lower module bearing and requires a different storage fixture.
